The graph of $y=ax^3+bx^2+cx+d$ is given below, where $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ are integers.  Find $d$.

[asy]
size(140);
Label f;

f.p=fontsize(4);

xaxis(-3,3,Ticks(f, 1.0));

yaxis(-4,4,Ticks(f, 1.0));

real f(real x)

{

return x^3-3x^2-2x+2;

}

draw(graph(f,-2.7,2.7),linewidth(1),Arrows(6));
[/asy]

Three congruent circles of radius 4 are arranged such that each circle is tangent to the other two circles. A smaller circle of radius $r$ is drawn inside the triangle formed by the centers of the three larger circles, so that it is tangent to all three sides of the triangle. What is the value of $r$?

[asy]
unitsize(1cm);
pair A = (0,0), B = (4,0), C = (2,2*sqrt(3));
filldraw(Circle((2,sqrt(3)),r),gray(0.7));
filldraw(Circle(A,4),white);
filldraw(Circle(B,4),white);
filldraw(Circle(C,4),white);
draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(2,2*sqrt(3))--cycle);
dot((0,0));
dot((4,0));
dot((2,2*sqrt(3)));
draw((2,sqrt(3))--(2.3,sqrt(3)),Arrow);
draw((2,sqrt(3))--(2.1,sqrt(3)+0.2),Arrow);
label("$r$",(2.1,sqrt(3)+0.1),N);
[/asy]

A square is inscribed in the ellipse
\[\frac{x^2}{3} + \frac{y^2}{6} = 1,\]so that its sides are parallel to the coordinate axes.  Find the area of the square.

[asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

draw(xscale(sqrt(3))*yscale(sqrt(6))*Circle((0,0),1));
draw((sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--(-sqrt(2),sqrt(2))--(-sqrt(2),-sqrt(2))--(sqrt(2),-sqrt(2))--cycle);
draw((-2,0)--(2,0));
draw((0,-3)--(0,3));
[/asy]
